meta {
  name: Update bill
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/bills/{{billId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "Updated via Bruno",
    "dueDate": "2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z"
  }
}

docs {
  Admin only. PATCH on a bill in PAID/REJECTED/ARCHIVED returns
  409 BILL_NOT_EDITABLE with `details.status`. Sending `null` on
  required-non-null fields (amount/currency/invoiceDate/dueDate) returns
  400 VALIDATION_ERROR.

  `paymentMethod` is consulted at approve time only. Editing it while
  the bill is DRAFT or PENDING_APPROVAL changes which rail the Payment
  is created with on approve. Editing it AFTER approve updates the
  bill column but does NOT affect the live Payment.method (which is
  the source of truth from approve onward); the UI locks the field at
  that point. Send `null` to clear the override and fall back to the
  vendor default. Example body lines:
      "paymentMethod": "WIRE"
      "paymentMethod": null
}
